  "releaseNotes": "NextGenSoftware.OASIS.API.Providers.PolygonOASIS v2.0.5\n\nConnects the OASIS to Polygon -- Ethereum's leading L2 scaling solution offering EVM compatibility, dramatically lower fees, and near-instant finality. Stores OASIS holons, avatars, and NFTs on Polygon PoS or zkEVM with full Ethereum interoperability. Part of the OASIS HOT-Swappable Provider Architecture -- 55+ networks. Ecosystem: https://oasisomniverse.one\n\nWhat's new since v2.0.4\n- Add runnable Polygon public balance CQL walkthrough and guide (ffbcbae)\n- Enroll Polygon read profile and verify native Mongo HTTP federation (e7da567)\n- MOVING DOCS AROUND (32a8004)\n- security: remove a committed testnet chain private key (and a block-explorer API key) from provider DNA files, test harness configs and .env; the Arbitrum test harness reads OASIS_TEST_CHAIN_PRIVATE_KEY instead. The key is still in git history: rotate it. (fefa98c)\n- Share EVM public CQL reader and add native Polygon balance profile (ad91c3c)\n- Verify encrypted Polygon provider roundtrip on reusable EVM (42e2855)\n\nFull changelog\nhttps://github.com/NextGenSoftwareUK/OASIS/commits/master/Providers/Blockchain/NextGenSoftware.OASIS.API.Providers.PolygonOASIS",
